WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.070 --> 00:00:06.460
Steve Kaplan: To go back to Connections, in
SPY Movie we have Melissa McCarthy meeting

00:00:06.460 --> 00:00:10.570
all sorts of people that are going to come
to help her.

00:00:10.570 --> 00:00:21.599
She meets Aldo who is this seemingly Italian
spy who is working for the CIA but who is

00:00:21.599 --> 00:00:27.140
always on the make and seemingly is always
trying to stick his tongue down Melissa McCarthy’s

00:00:27.140 --> 00:00:28.140
throat.

00:00:28.140 --> 00:00:34.172
Her friend Nancy, who is there helping her
from the basement in Langley (Virginia - CIA

00:00:34.172 --> 00:00:43.440
headquarters) shows up in Rome and is going
to help her deal with all her missions as

00:00:43.440 --> 00:00:47.199
she’s trying to retrieve the nuclear bomb.

00:00:47.199 --> 00:00:55.680
Even Rayna who is seemingly her nemesis (played
brilliantly by Rose Byrne) turns out (in the

00:00:55.680 --> 00:00:58.740
end) in fact be another ally.

00:00:58.740 --> 00:01:06.030
So in Connections is the part of the movie
in which your protagonist not only is moving

00:01:06.030 --> 00:01:12.880
outside their comfort zone, becoming a more
actualized, more complete person.

00:01:12.880 --> 00:01:23.000
But they are able to reach out and create
new relationships on a new basis.

00:01:23.000 --> 00:01:27.740
One of the things that I do want to talk about
in terms of the Normal World, one of the things

00:01:27.740 --> 00:01:33.780
I didn’t mention yet is that in the Normal
World your protagonist has flawed or absent

00:01:33.780 --> 00:01:36.430
relationships.

00:01:36.430 --> 00:01:40.100
Bill Murray (GROUNDHOG DAY) doesn’t have
a girlfriend, he doesn’t really respect

00:01:40.100 --> 00:01:43.990
women.

00:01:43.990 --> 00:01:52.040
Ben Stiller in TROPIC THUNDER, his only relationship
is his agent and even that is just kind of

00:01:52.040 --> 00:02:00.420
somebody to get him a tebow to be sent to
this jungle where he’s shooting this movie.

00:02:00.420 --> 00:02:03.780
And of course, Melissa McCarthy (SPY) has
no relationships.

00:02:03.780 --> 00:02:10.940
She pines for Jude Law and we can see from
an earlier scene where Jude Law takes her

00:02:10.940 --> 00:02:20.450
out to dinner to thank her for being such
a good helper back in the CIA basement.

00:02:20.450 --> 00:02:28.800
That’s where he kind of gives her this terrible
crazy cupcake piece of jewelry, because we

00:02:28.800 --> 00:02:33.740
can see that he doesn’t really see her as
an equal.

00:02:33.740 --> 00:02:41.780
So in the Connections part of the Comic Hero’s
Journey, because your character is transforming,

00:02:41.780 --> 00:02:47.240
your character is growing, and again, without
them knowing it, we the audience can see it,

00:02:47.240 --> 00:02:51.090
but they’re still not aware of it.

00:02:51.090 --> 00:02:57.820
That is when these unexpected allies and also
unexpected enemies can come out.

00:02:57.820 --> 00:03:04.670
That’s the part of the movie where Melissa
McCarthy realizes that Karen Walker, whom

00:03:04.670 --> 00:03:10.040
she idolized, who was a star femme fatale
spy at the CIA, was really a double agent.

00:03:10.040 --> 00:03:11.040
QUESTION FOR THE VIEWERS: Think of any comedy
movie, does the main character have any flawed

00:03:11.040 --> 00:03:11.046
or absent relationships in the beginning?

